{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdNzvzyAVr9JzKhKxhKet","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fhs2rgXQ5FkvMFywwMqa3K","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.eYRrwo/SOLUTION.md","content":"# Solution\n\nTwo bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:\n\n1. **`get` did not count as a \"use\".** On a hit it returned the value without\n   calling `move_to_end`, so the entry kept its original insertion position in\n   the `OrderedDict`. A key that had just been read was still treated as the\n   least recently used and got evicted by the next `put`. Fixed by moving the\n   key to the end before returning.\n\n2. **`put` evicted on updates to existing keys.** The capacity check was\n   `len(self._data) >= self.capacity` with no test for key membership, so\n   overwriting an already-present key at full capacity popped the oldest entry\n   even though the dict size wasn't going to grow. Fixed by only evicting when\n   the key is new.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":160,"cache_read_input_tokens":22656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":72,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"375088e9-3a3e-47a9-8226-02e678450dca","uuid":"44390487-be37-4ff2-930d-77ac1c2b0ca7","timestamp":"2026-07-25T15:18:45.181Z","request_id":"req_011CdNzvz9ZQ75Yy2kHi8rwV"}
